# Chroma content pack Stage and Screen: WORLD-ONLY moments (moments 66 to 73 of MOMENTS-BRIEF.md, Part 5): four that
# belong to the tribal world and four that belong to the magic world (stage/worlds.py, WORLD_ONLY_STAGE). Syntax: header
# of chroma-library/build.py. Rules: library-spec.md and the brief's pack rules. Names in title:, grants:, drops:,
# requires:, holds: and aims: come from stage/catalogue.py, core/reach.py and the base catalogue. Each moment carries
# `only:` and that world's line alone; its labels and scenes are written for that world (scene tribal ..., scene magic
# ...), so the game tells them only there.
# Each life event is even on its own (one mean chance for every means color): alpha even, stakes 1.0, the five one-color
# options plus the combination set named in its header comment. Each world's four moments use both halves of two
# combination lines (tribal: D5 triads and D2 pairs; magic: D6 triads and D1 pairs), so the pack stays color-even in
# every world. Parts carry their real chances, the same for every color inside a moment where the moment allows it; the
# earned-odds lifts (helps.py, half on the lead) come on top in the engine. A lead for someone who may not hold an
# actor's title is `title: lead actor or actress; professional actor`, the lead first; the amateur lead is
# `grants: a lead role to remember`. Each world has its crossing to the lead: the great mask (68) in the tribal world,
# the night of the dead (71) and the glamour (72) in the magic world.
# The tribal world has no magic (library-spec.md): the spirits and the shaman are how the band tells its stories, and
# nothing here says a spirit truly acts. In the magic world every supernatural way is one choice among ordinary ones,
# and each has a price (a mark, a binding, a closed: line with a backfire). Round 5, 2026-10-07: no act here rests on
# the person's own gift (gift awakening is held for a later version, and the catalogue has no name for one): the magic
# comes from someone else (the company's medium, a hedge-witch, an illusionist), which anyone in the magic world can
# try, and the town's or the Order's disapproval is a `closed: approval:` line with a backfire.
# Children act only in supervised forms: these moments start at 16 (past school-leaving age) or 18, and a child in the
# illusionists' fairy scene plays with a parent's leave and a chaperone beside it. No real person, production, theatre,
# studio, film, award, agency or union is named. per_year is the yearly rate per eligible person (whoever holds a title
# or perk in holds:, and everyone of age in the magic world for 70); every figure is an estimate.
# Round 5, 2026-10-07 (checklist P14, value tags): 4 options in this file retagged so the v: values read one of the
# option's own colors (check.py section 4): White's by-the-book singles lead with conformity (not conformity with
# achievement, which reads Blue), Red's singles on impulse lead with stimulation or hedonism (not self-direction,
# which reads Black), Green's singles of home and kin with tradition and benevolence or universalism (not security,
# which reads White), and Red's kindness on the spot with benevolence and stimulation; plus the largest
# disagreements check.py listed (an old custom asked: tradition and conformity; family first: benevolence and
# tradition; kin led away from the chief: self-direction and tradition; a day's pay weighed: power).

# ================================================================ tribal world
# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 66. the old teller dies at midwinter (triads D5a)
# A door: the band needs a new voice. Every one-color way is a try for the teller-player's place (title: professional
# actor, the band's form of it) at the same real chance; the triads are the other answers: a night of trials, standing
# aside for the apprentice, teaching the children, new tellings, the shaman's word.
# The band asks its players of two winters or more (an amateur actor, or an old teller's apprentice): the rung below.
# Round 5, 2026-10-07 (checklist P9): at 5, each try for the teller's place is a long shot (a bold try at the next
# rung) and carries `grants_if_fails: a long shot that missed`.

== the old teller dies at midwinter
tier: life event
only: tribal
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 16-95
holds: amateur actor | drama school student
tenure: 2-100
per_year: 0 .01 .02 .02 .02 .03
drivers: harsh+.2
times: per player of the band of two winters or more (an amateur actor, or an old teller's apprentice) in the tribal world a year: about 1 in 50, when a band's teller dies or grows too old (estimate)
likelier: a hard winter, an old teller who never named an apprentice, a player who sat at the old one's side
rarer: a band with several tellers, a young teller already in place, a player who keeps to the edge of the firelight
gap: 5-10
tone: mixed
life: community, meaning
horizon: months
roles: elder, mentor, rival, friend, child
tribal: the old teller dies in the long nights, and the fire is silent where the stories were
scene tribal: The old teller dies in the deepest of the long nights, and the band lays her masks beside her. Since then the fire has been silent where the stories were, and every evening the children ask who will tell them now.
scene tribal W: {N} sat at the old one's side for years and knows how each telling must go, word for word and night by night. Someone has to keep them as they were given.
scene tribal U: {N} has heard every story told a dozen ways. The old teller changed them a little each winter, and {N} wants to know which parts were the bones and which the skin.
scene tribal B: Whoever takes the teller's place will sit near the elders and be fed first after the hunt. Across the fire, {rival} is plainly thinking the same.
scene tribal R: The silence at the fire is more than {N} can stand. Ready or not, {N} wants to get up in the firelight and fill it.
scene tribal G: The stories belong to the band, not to any one voice. {N} thinks of the old teller's hands, and of the little ones who have never heard the winter tellings to the end.
- W | keep every telling exactly as the old teller gave it, night after night | title: professional actor | grants_if_fails: a long shot that missed | identity | v: tradition, conformity | chance: 5
- U | piece the tellings together from what every old one remembers, and tell them whole | title: professional actor | grants_if_fails: a long shot that missed | mark: learned a skill | v: self-direction, universalism | chance: 5
- B | ask the elders for the teller's place, and the teller's share of every hunt | title: professional actor | grants_if_fails: a long shot that missed | v: power, achievement | chance: 5
- R | stand up at the silent fire the first night, and tell the bear story by heart | title: professional actor | grants_if_fails: a long shot that missed | aims: professional actor | v: stimulation, self-direction | chance: 5
- G | keep the stories alive through the winter, until a younger voice is ready | title: professional actor | grants_if_fails: a long shot that missed | binds | identity | v: benevolence, tradition | chance: 5
- WUR | ask the elders for a night of trials, and tell a piece of your own there | grants: telling a story aloud | door | v: universalism, stimulation | chance: 70
- WRG | stand aside, and ask the band to give the place to the old one's apprentice | mark: turned down a chance | self_control: + | v: benevolence, tradition | chance: 70
- WBG | teach the band's children the tellings, as the old ones always have | title: drama teacher | requires: telling a story aloud | without: approval | lacking: .5 | v: tradition, benevolence | chance: 70
- UBR | make new tellings of your own, and play them at the summer gathering | grants: writing scripts | identity | v: self-direction, achievement | chance: 70
- UBG | ask the shaman quietly whom the old teller meant to follow her | v: tradition, security | chance: 70
works: By the next new moon the fire has its stories again, and the band settles close to listen.
works: The elders nod over how it was settled, and the children fall asleep to the old tellings once more.
fails: The band cannot agree, and for the rest of the winter the fire stays half silent.
fails: {rival} speaks first and loudest, and the elders give the stories to another voice.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 67. the spirits ride the dancer (triads D5b)
# A fall. The band reads the trance as a spirit, and nothing says one came: the options are the band's answers, and
# the lead is lost (Green steps back) or played as never before (the WBR triad, only for whoever wears the great mask).
# The chances differ by act; they are set so every color's mean is the same.

== the spirits ride the dancer
tier: life event
only: tribal
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-95
holds: professional actor | lead actor or actress | amateur actor
per_year: 0 0 .01 .01 .01 .01
drivers: harsh+.3
times: per player in the tribal world a year: about 1 in 100 (estimate)
likelier: a long fast before the telling, a hard season that makes the band fearful, a player who gives everything to the deep tellings
rarer: a shaman who knows the player well, light tellings for the children, a player who keeps a little back
gap: 5-10
tone: trouble
life: community, meaning
horizon: months
roles: elder, friend, rival
tribal: in the deepest telling the fire roars, you speak in a voice that is not yours, and the band draws back
scene tribal: In the deepest telling of the winter the fire roars up, and {N} speaks in a voice nobody knows, old and slow, for as long as it takes a log to burn through. When it ends the band has drawn back from the light, and the shaman cannot say what it was.
scene tribal W: There is a rite for everything that comes out of the dark. {N} wants this put right the proper way, before the band's fear hardens into something worse.
scene tribal U: {N} remembers almost nothing, only heat and a long fall. A fast, the smoke, three nights without sleep: there may be plain reasons, and {N} wants to find them.
scene tribal B: Since that night the young ones look at {N} with awe, and even the elders lower their eyes. Fear is a kind of power, and {N} can feel it.
scene tribal R: Whatever happened at the fire, {N} has never felt so alive. Part of {N} wants to go back into it, whatever the band says.
scene tribal G: The band's peace matters more than any telling. {N} sees the mothers pulling the children close, and {friend} keeping to the far side of the fire.
- W | go through the shaman's cleansing rite, and fast as long as he says | self_control: + | v: tradition, conformity | chance: 67
- U | tell the band plainly that it was the fast and the smoke, nothing more | identity | v: self-direction, universalism | chance: 60
- B | let the band believe the first ancestor spoke, and take the seat nearest the fire | closed: approval: claiming the ancestor's voice; backfire: the shaman says no ancestor spoke, and the band turns away | self_control: - | v: power | chance: 65
- R | go back into the trance at the next telling, and let it take hold | mark: took a wild risk | closed: approval: a trance the shaman has forbidden; backfire: the band casts the player out for a season | v: stimulation, hedonism | chance: 67
- G | step back from the great tellings, and dance only in the herd for a year | drops: lead actor or actress | v: security, tradition | chance: 60
- WUG | sit with the shaman and the oldest dancers until they agree on what it was | door | v: tradition, universalism | chance: 65
- WUB | dance the deep tellings only with the shaman beside the fire, by his rule | binds | v: conformity, security | chance: 70
- WBR | wear the great mask at the gathering, and let the trance into the ancestor's dance | grants: good notices | requires: lead actor or actress | without: impossible | mark: took a wild risk | v: achievement, stimulation | chance: 45
- URG | go alone into the hills for three days, and come back knowing what it was | body: heavy | identity | v: self-direction, universalism | chance: 65
- BRG | take the family to another band, where nobody saw that night | mark: left home | moves: yes | v: security, self-direction | chance: 70
works: By the spring the band's fear has eased, and {N} is welcome at the fire again.
works: The elders settle it among themselves, and the talk of that night turns from fear to wonder.
fails: The fear does not ease, and families move their sleeping hides further from {Ns} fire.
fails: {rival} keeps the whispering alive all winter, and the elders begin to look the other way.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 68. chosen to wear the great mask (pairs D2a)
# The tribal crossing to the lead. The band puts the person forward, but the elders of every clan choose one wearer
# by the last night, so each one-color way to the mask is at the same chance (15) for one of the band's players,
# and three tenths of it for an amateur player of five winters with a lead behind them (the one rung skipped;
# LIFE_STAGE, no one else is put forward); Red's carries the mask's price
# (a wild risk, and a binding). The pairs turn the mask down, give it to another, or ask what it takes.

